-- domain `std`: Modal's standard library, in Modal (docs/std.md). The compiler reads it only
-- when a program imports std; it needs none of it to build, and none of it uses C's libc.
-- What this file binds is std's face: `assert := import("std").assert`.
--
-- Two names are still the compiler's, reached by their old paths until Modal can write them
-- (docs/std.md §4): `import("std").io.print` (variadic over types) and `import("std").sys.put`
-- (the target's byte sink).
version := "0.1.0"

assert := import("./debug").assert
